items.body:
Reconciles the accepted M23.5 benchmark-contract implementation.

- records implementation exact head and merge SHA;
- records all-green accepted-head CI;
- confirms BGE-M3 is selected only for non-production pilot use;
- confirms lexical remains authoritative;
- confirms Qdrant write, R2/pointer mutation, Source mutation and production traffic change are all false.

Production mutation dispatched: false.

## What changed

### Metric corrections
- excludes `key_highlights_for_candidate` from macro extraction F1 because it is a generated recommendation field rather than a direct extraction target;
- keeps that field visible under `unscored_fields` for later human or semantic review;
- normalizes documented acronym and expanded-form equivalents such as NLP, RAG, LLM, API, ML, DL and CV;
- preserves semantic modifiers so `responsible AI` does not become equivalent to `agentic AI`;
- reports accuracy/F1 by individual field in addition to aggregate scores;
- records evaluation protocol version `1.1.0` separately from dataset version.

### Contract-type guardrail
- explicitly prevents the model from inferring `contract_type` from words inside the role title;
- requires `Unknown` unless the offer states the employment or contract type.

### Stratified five-case smoke suite
- adds a dedicated bilingual smoke dataset rather than taking the first five rows of the full benchmark;
- covers English and French;
- covers five distinct categories;
- covers easy, medium and hard cases;
- includes missing contract/start-date cases and conflicting location context.

### Workflow and validation
- the `5` GitHub Actions option now runs `evaluation/job_offers.smoke.v1.jsonl`;
- the `50` option continues to run the frozen full Benchmark V1;
- benchmark integrity validation now checks smoke-suite language, category and difficulty coverage;
- adds regression tests for acronym equivalence, semantic-modifier preservation, unscored recommendations and contract inference guardrails.

## Evidence from the first run

Re-scoring the uploaded five-case report with the corrected extraction protocol yields list-field F1 of 1.0 on all five cases. The original 0.7111 was depressed by acronym formatting and by scoring recommendation text against short skill labels. The scalar error on `offer_004` remains a real model error and is addressed through the contract-type prompt guardrail.

## Interpretation boundary

The full 50-offer V1 dataset remains synthetic and English-only. The new smoke suite provides bilingual coverage for preflight validation but does not make the full benchmark bilingual or externally representative.

Closes #380.

## What changed

- adds a governed parent-article gold overlay without weakening the existing M20 exact-section contract;
- separates threshold calibration and held-out evaluation over the immutable 107-document / 16-query vectors;
- adds a zero-network offline rebenchmark CLI and deterministic decision receipts;
- selects Cloudflare `@cf/baai/bge-m3` for a non-production pilot while keeping `RETRIEVAL_MODE=lexical`;
- rejects fixed RRF as the preferred candidate;
- records that production abstention is not yet accepted;
- normalizes provider vectors explicitly;
- supports the actual Qdrant named vector `default` and adds read-only collection preflight before any explicit write.

## Safety

- no Cloudflare call in this PR;
- no Qdrant point write;
- no R2 or pointer mutation;
- no Source mutation and no merge of Source PR #19;
- no production traffic or retrieval-default change;
- Graph Neural Retrieval remains forbidden.

Production mutation dispatched: false.

## Summary

Start the next roadmap-defined Phase O optimization cycle from verified `main` `31a33f5e7193dda5ab777c079154ec5ee49ddf4b` by recording the mandatory bottleneck hypothesis and exact accepted baseline before implementing another kernel candidate.

- records the exact M45 Thor/Vulkan grouped-forward measurements and provenance;
- states explicitly that those measurements compare portable grouped vs `Q4Vec4Grouped`, not SciRust legacy multi-dispatch, so they do not by themselves close the 1.0 Definition-of-Done comparison;
- selects the roadmap-prioritized GQA-specific K/V reuse hypothesis for the next isolated candidate;
- defines correctness, benchmark, fallback and rejection criteria before coding;
- keeps routing unchanged and `performance_claim=none` beyond the cited exact-device evidence.

Sovereignty remains Rust-native host + WGPU/WGSL only. No project-authored C/C++, C ABI bridge, mandatory CUDA C++/nvcc, WMMA/WGMMA, CUTLASS, cuDNN, or vendor SDK is introduced.
